+ ExperimentalOpt into features that are still being evaluated before they become default behavior.Experimental features may break at any time.These features are opt-in and come with no compatibility guarantees. They may change, break, or be removed without notice. Avoid relying on them for critical or production workflows.Experimental featuresOptional product features that are still being evaluated.Agent ChatExperimentalTalk to each agent in one ongoing conversation. Clarify goals and create tasks for execution.Turning this off preserves conversations and lets active runs finish, but prevents new messages.Beta skillsExperimentalAllow agents to pin beta releases of the Blentera core skill. Disabling this returns every agent to the default live skill without removing saved pins.Blentera RunnerExperimentalAllow new Codex agents to select the experimental Rust Blentera Runner, including authenticated runner ingress when a sandbox requires it. Onboarding continues to use legacy adapters. Turning this off hides the choice without affecting existing native runs.Built-in AgentsExperimentalShow Blentera-managed built-in agent surfaces, including built-in roster badges, the Built-in agents tab, and built-in agent setup controls.CasesExperimentalDurable work products (blog posts, tweet storms…) that tasks create and iterate on. Adds the Cases tab and the agent case API.Turning Cases off hides the tab and blocks the case API; existing case data is kept.Chat connectorsExperimentalConnect agents to Slack, GitHub, Discord, Microsoft Teams, and Telegram conversations.Turning this off hides chat setup, channels, and connected-task controls. Existing chat connections keep running. GitHub and other tool connectors stay available.DecisionsExperimentalShow the Decisions item in the main sidebar — the attention home that surfaces the tasks awaiting your input — while the surface is still being evaluated.Enable EnvironmentsExperimentalShow environment management in company settings and allow project and agent environment assignment controls.Enable External ObjectsExperimentalDetect external URLs in issues and show resolved status for pull requests, tickets, and other referenced work objects.Enable Isolated WorkspacesExperimentalShow execution workspace controls in project configuration and allow isolated workspace behavior for new and existing task runs.Experimental File ViewerExperimentalShow task detail controls for browsing and previewing workspace files relative to a task.First task: propose with a plan documentExperimentalWhen the user's first request is a single task, the chief of staff writes a short plan document and a checkbox card instead of a one-card confirmation. Applies to organizations created after the toggle is flipped.Memory connectorsExperimentalConnect Mem0, Zep, Supermemory, Cognee, and Honcho for long-term memory and context.Turning this off hides setup for these connectors. Existing connections keep running.Simplified English InteractionsExperimentalInstruct agents to write user interactions (plan confirmations, questions, suggested tasks, checkbox prompts) in ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English, with brief context on what information the decision needs and what happens for each choice.Status CardsExperimentalEnable the experimental shared status-card board and its gated API. Existing card data is kept when this is disabled.Enabling Status Cards also enables Summaries.Streamlined UIExperimentalUse the simplified main sidebar, shared Tasks and Inbox presentation, focused task detail layout, and contextual navigation across Agents, Routines, Skills, and Settings.Turning this off restores the legacy shell and navigation. Task and page data are unchanged.SummariesExperimentalShow Summarizer-generated status slots on project and workspace pages, with on-demand refresh and revision history. Existing summary data is kept when this is disabled.Status Cards requires Summaries. Disabling Summaries also disables Status Cards.V5 agent runtime and project controlAll V5 features default off. Review current authorization, provider qualification and rollback before enabling them.Agent identitiesInternalStable logical agent identities and home organizations.Owner: Instance administrator. Rollback disables this feature and its dependent behavior while retaining immutable data.Agent runtime fabricInternalServer-built immutable execution manifests.Owner: Instance administrator. Enable required features first: enableFoundationV1, enableContextEngineV1, agent_identities_v5, agent_provider_bindings_v5. Rollback disables this feature and its dependent behavior while retaining immutable data.Autonomous Skill promotionInternalExplicitly governed promotion after all evaluation gates.Owner: Instance administrator. Enable required features first: skill_autonomous_proposals_v5. Rollback disables this feature and its dependent behavior while retaining immutable data.Autonomous Skill proposalsInternalPolicy-bound private/proposed Skill candidates.Owner: Instance administrator. Enable required features first: skill_lifecycle_v5. Rollback disables this feature and its dependent behavior while retaining immutable data.Company presencesInternalIndependent local agent authority in multiple companies.Owner: Instance administrator. Enable required features first: agent_identities_v5. Rollback disables this feature and its dependent behavior while retaining immutable data.Company relationshipsInternalAccepted company relationships that confer no access.Owner: Instance administrator. Rollback disables this feature and its dependent behavior while retaining immutable data.Cross-company executionInternalExplicit delegated scopes with local authorization and provenance.Owner: Instance administrator. Enable required features first: enableFoundationV1, enableContextEngineV1, agent_multi_company_presence_v5, agent_provider_bindings_v5. Rollback disables this feature and its dependent behavior while retaining immutable data.Organization unitsInternalLocal organization units with human and agent memberships.Owner: Instance administrator. Enable required features first: agent_identities_v5. Rollback disables this feature and its dependent behavior while retaining immutable data.Plan versus actualInternalBaseline comparisons using observed execution facts.Owner: Instance administrator. Enable required features first: project_roadmap_v5. Rollback disables this feature and its dependent behavior while retaining immutable data.Playbook projectionInternalCandidate-only Playbook-to-Skill projection and reviewed feedback.Owner: Instance administrator. Enable required features first: playbooks_v5, skill_lifecycle_v5. Rollback disables this feature and its dependent behavior while retaining immutable data.PlaybooksInternalReviewed canonical procedures with immutable revisions.Owner: Instance administrator. Rollback disables this feature and its dependent behavior while retaining immutable data.Portfolio capability sharingInternalPinned publish, install, subscribe and fork with local governance.Owner: Instance administrator. Enable required features first: skill_lifecycle_v5, company_relationships_v5. Rollback disables this feature and its dependent behavior while retaining immutable data.Portfolio viewInternalPer-company authorized aggregation for Portfolio and August OS.Owner: Instance administrator. Rollback disables this feature and its dependent behavior while retaining immutable data.Project forecastInternalSeparate forecasts and optimistic planning proposals.Owner: Instance administrator. Enable required features first: project_roadmap_v5. Rollback disables this feature and its dependent behavior while retaining immutable data.Project RoadmapInternalCanonical task planning, milestones and explicit baselines.Owner: Instance administrator. Rollback disables this feature and its dependent behavior while retaining immutable data.Provider bindingsInternalScoped provider profiles, sessions and capability contracts.Owner: Instance administrator. Enable required features first: agent_identities_v5. Rollback disables this feature and its dependent behavior while retaining immutable data.Role PacksInternalVersioned role requirements that never grant permissions.Owner: Instance administrator. Enable required features first: agent_runtime_fabric_v5. Rollback disables this feature and its dependent behavior while retaining immutable data.Shared trusted runtimeInternalExplicitly acknowledged reduced isolation in provider-local state.Owner: Instance administrator. Enable required features first: agent_provider_bindings_v5. Rollback disables this feature and its dependent behavior while retaining immutable data.Skill lifecycleInternalImmutable active Skills, challengers, evaluations and revalidation.Owner: Instance administrator. Rollback disables this feature and its dependent behavior while retaining immutable data.Skill resolverInternalDeterministic authorized Skill selection and context budgets.Owner: Instance administrator. Enable required features first: agent_runtime_fabric_v5, role_packs_v5. Rollback disables this feature and its dependent behavior while retaining immutable data.Blentera Developer ModeInternal tools for developing, testing, and debugging Blentera.Auto-Restart Dev Server When IdleExperimentalIn `pnpm dev:once`, wait for all queued and running local agent runs to finish, then restart the server automatically when backend changes or migrations make the current boot stale.Blentera Developer ModeExperimentalShow internal Blentera maintainer tools and observability links, including Honeycomb trace queries on run pages.Managed Environment OnlyExperimentalHide the local environment and run all agents in the platform-managed environment.Server Info Debug ViewExperimentalShow a "Server" section in the account drawer with the current server restart time and running commit.Smoke LabExperimentalAdd a "Smoke Lab" tab under Apps → Developer and an "Integration smoke" card on the dashboard for exercising every integration path against deterministic local fixtures (fake OAuth provider + loopback MCP servers). Private (non-public) deployments only.Task Plan DecompositionExperimentalShow accepted-plan decomposition history on task detail pages. Intended for debugging and validating subtask creation behavior while the presentation is still being refined.LegacyThese features are going to be removed.Classic Task InterfaceExperimentalRestores the previous task detail page: the page-level header with inline description editing, the plain comment thread, and the fixed Properties sidebar. Chat-only features — streaming activity folding, inline plan and question cards, the three-mode composer — are unavailable in the classic view.Switching takes effect immediately. No task data is affected.Goals Sidebar LinkExperimentalRestore the Goals item in the main sidebar while the goals surface is being evaluated.Capability lifecycle registryFull record from the shared capability catalog. Blank or unqualified fields have not been qualified; they do not mean a capability or its data is absent.A2UI adapterInternalOptional bounded catalog compatibility.SupportNo compatibility guaranteeOwnerAugust Works platform operatorCustomer surfacesNot mapped yetExperience profilesNot mapped yetEntitlementNot mapped yetCriticalityUnqualifiedData categoriesNot mapped yetService dependenciesNot mapped yetDocs / helpNot linkedHuman support and HelpOpen HelpRelease evidenceNot linkedDeprecationNot scheduledSunsetNot scheduledReplacementNot recordedMigration guideNot linkedLast reviewedNot recordedGA security / privacyUnqualifiedGA accessibilityUnqualifiedGA operabilityUnqualifiedGA migration planUnqualifiedGA criticality evidenceUnqualifiedCustomer action cardsInternalBounded typed UI; canonical authorization at execution time.SupportNo compatibility guaranteeOwnerAugust Works platform operatorCustomer surfacesNot mapped yetExperience profilesNot mapped yetEntitle